From cf5f15390515b6fd131b94e4b6243b9e00feae8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:07:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): cut session_tasks read overhead [daveey]

Profiling 12 session_tasks calls on hermes-hub: most CPU went to opening and
closing read-only sqlite connections through kanban_lockguard, not to queries.

- kanban_origin.gateway_name: memoize this gateway's own name for 10 min,
  keyed on hub.db's file identity (path, dev, inode) and the mail config
  signature, never on the WAL/mtime the hub writes continuously. Gateways are
  never renamed in place; re-enrollment replaces hub.db (new inode) and busts
  it. gateway_names (the known set) keeps its 5 s memo.
- kanban_ro_batch: inside session_tasks and the links projection, every
  kanban_origin._ro of the same file borrows one shared read-only connection,
  closed when the call ends. A borrow's close rolls back and resets
  row_factory; a file already borrowed, or a batch inherited from another
  thread, gets a private connection, so semantics match a fresh open.
- preserve_origin_obligations: run the cheap released/unfinished/gateway
  filters before the five-field check; same result (equivalence test against
  the old filter).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
